screen.SHADOWS=Shadows
screen.SHADOWS.comment=Sun and moon shadows. Shadow Distance has the biggest performance impact (it re-renders the world from the sun).
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Sharpness of shadows. 4096 is a good balance; 8192 costs noticeably more VRAM and fill rate.
option.shadowDistance=§eShadow Distance§r
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from you shadows are drawn. Higher values re-render more of the world from the sun's view (CPU and GPU cost).
value.shadowDistance.64.0=4 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.96.0=6 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.128.0=8 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.160.0=10 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.192.0=12 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.224.0=14 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.256.0=16 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.320.0=20 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.384.0=24 Chunks
value.shadowDistance.512.0=32 Chunks
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Minimum Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Blur of shadow edges right where an object touches the ground (they soften further out by Sun Size).
option.SHADOW_PENUMBRA=Sun Size
option.SHADOW_PENUMBRA.comment=Shadows are sharp where an object meets the ground and soften the further they fall from it, like under the real sun; much softer in overcast weather. 0 = always sharp.
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES=Shadow Samples
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES.comment=Samples of the soft shadow filter (half as many far away). More: smoother soft shadows, a little slower.
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS=Contact Shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Tiny shadows the shadow map is too coarse for: grass on the ground, small items, where mobs stand. Traced on screen within about 24 blocks.
option.FAR_SHADOWS=Far Shadows
option.FAR_SHADOWS.comment=Shadows beyond the shadow distance from a coarse height map of the terrain: distant mountains shade each other, valleys go dark at sunset. Draws more of the world in the shadow pass (some CPU/GPU cost).
option.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE=Far Shadow Range
option.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.comment=How far far shadows reach, in multiples of the shadow distance (never beyond the render distance, nor ~500 blocks). Higher costs more.
value.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.1.5=1.5x
value.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.2.0=2x
value.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.3.0=3x
value.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.4.0=4x
value.FAR_SHADOW_RANGE.6.0=6x
option.TRANSLUCENT_ENTITY_SHADOWS=See-through Mob Shadows
option.TRANSLUCENT_ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment=See-through mobs and their see-through parts (slimes, ...) cast partial shadows instead of solid ones.
option.LIGHTNING_SHADOWS=Lightning Shadows
option.LIGHTNING_SHADOWS.comment=Lightning casts hard shadows from hills, trees and buildings for an instant. Needs Coloured Lighting.
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS=§eEntity Shadows§r
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment=Mobs and players cast shadows (within a quarter of the shadow distance). Block entities like chests never do, for performance.
option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Shadows
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Light through stained glass is tinted instead of blocked.
option.FOLIAGE_SSS=Leaf Translucency
option.FOLIAGE_SSS.comment=Sunlight passing through leaves and grass, strongest when looking towards the sun.

