screen.WEATHER=Weather
screen.WEATHER.comment=Storm clouds, lightning, rain and snow, storms, puddles and wet surfaces.
option.RAIN_OVERCAST=Overcast in Rain
option.RAIN_OVERCAST.comment=The clouds thicken into an overcast sky as it starts to rain, and clear up afterwards.
option.STORM_DARKNESS=Thunderstorm Darkness
option.STORM_DARKNESS.comment=How much darker the sky and its light get in a thunderstorm, with heavier storm clouds.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH=Lightning Flash
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment=How brightly lightning lights up its surroundings, the clouds and the sky for a moment.
option.RAIN_STYLE=Rain Style
value.RAIN_STYLE.0=Light & Warmer
value.RAIN_STYLE.1=Heavy & Colder
option.WEATHER_OPACITY=Rain & Snow Opacity
option.WEATHER_OPACITY.comment=Opacity of the rain and snow.
option.WEATHER_STORMS=Snowstorms & Sandstorms
option.WEATHER_STORMS.comment=While it rains, snowy biomes get a snowstorm and deserts and badlands a sandstorm: thick, coloured air.
option.PUDDLES=Puddles
option.PUDDLES.comment=Water collecting on flat ground under the open sky, mirroring the sky and clouds.
value.PUDDLES.0=Off
value.PUDDLES.1=In Rain
value.PUDDLES.2=Full Coverage in Rain
value.PUDDLES.3=Always
option.WET_SURFACES=Wet Surfaces
option.WET_SURFACES.comment=Surfaces out in the rain darken and get a slight sheen, drying slowly afterwards.
option.RAIN_RIPPLES=Rain Ripples
option.RAIN_RIPPLES.comment=Raindrops make rings on puddles and water.
screen.WAVING=Waving
screen.WAVING.comment=Plants, leaves, lily pads, lava, rain and the held item moving.
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_LEAVES=Waving Leaves & Vines
option.WAVING_LILY_PADS=Bobbing Lily Pads
option.WAVING_LAVA=Flowing Lava
option.WAVING_LAVA.comment=Lava's surface slowly churns.
option.WAVING_WEATHER=Slanted Rain & Snow
option.WAVING_WEATHER.comment=Rain and snow fall at an angle in the wind, more in thunderstorms.
option.NO_WAVING_INDOORS=No Waving Indoors
option.NO_WAVING_INDOORS.comment=Plants with no sky light above them stay still.
option.WAVING_SPEED=Waving Speed
option.WAVING_INTENSITY=Waving Intensity
option.WAVING_RAIN=Waving in Rain
option.WAVING_RAIN.comment=How much more plants wave while it rains.
option.HAND_SWAY=Hand Sway
option.HAND_SWAY.comment=The held item drifts gently, as if breathing.
value.HAND_SWAY.0=Off
value.HAND_SWAY.1=Subtle
value.HAND_SWAY.2=Normal
value.HAND_SWAY.3=Intense
option.BIOME_WATER=Biome Water
option.BIOME_WATER.comment=Water looks different per biome: rich deep blue and clearer in cold places, murky green in swamps, pale and clear in deserts, tropical turquoise in warm oceans, and more.

# ---- Pre-M10 additions
option.SSAO=Ambient Occlusion
option.SSAO.comment=Soft contact shadows in corners, where blocks meet, under overhangs and around mobs, and the sky light steered towards where the most sky is seen. Bright surfaces lose less light to it and keep their colour. Darkens only the ambient, bounced and block light, never sunlight.
value.SSAO.0=Off
value.SSAO.1=Medium
value.SSAO.2=High
option.SSAO_STRENGTH=Ambient Occlusion Strength
option.BLOCKLIGHT_FLICKER=Block Light Flickering
option.BLOCKLIGHT_FLICKER.comment=Torch and fire light breathes gently. Each step is 2% of the brightness.
value.BLOCKLIGHT_FLICKER.0=Off
option.PLAYER_SHADOW=Player Shadow
option.PLAYER_SHADOW.comment=Your own shadow. With Entity Shadows off, it is the only entity shadow drawn.
option.PLAYER_SHADOW_QUALITY=Player Shadow Quality
option.PLAYER_SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=Sharper shadows close to you, your own shadow especially: finer filtering near the player and a little more shadow detail around you (at the cost of a little detail far away).
value.PLAYER_SHADOW_QUALITY.0=Normal
value.PLAYER_SHADOW_QUALITY.1=High
value.PLAYER_SHADOW_QUALITY.2=Very High
option.LEAF_SHADOW_OPTIMIZATION=Leaf Shadow Optimization
option.LEAF_SHADOW_OPTIMIZATION.comment=Leaves and vines in caves and interiors (with almost no sky light) cast no shadows, where they hardly ever show. A little faster.
option.NO_CLOUDS_UNDERGROUND=No Clouds Underground
option.NO_CLOUDS_UNDERGROUND.comment=Skips the volumetric clouds while you are deep underground, where the sky cannot be seen. Faster in caves.
option.DISTANT_LIGHT_BLOOM=Distant Light Bloom
option.DISTANT_LIGHT_BLOOM.comment=At night and in caves, far-away lights glow a little wider, as if scattered by the air in between.
value.DISTANT_LIGHT_BLOOM.0.00=Off

# ---- W1: world state
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Auto Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=The image adapts to how bright the view is, like eyes: caves and nights get a bit brighter over a few seconds, bright snow and sunlit views a bit darker. Only part of the way, so dark places still look dark.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_STRENGTH=Auto Exposure Strength
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_STRENGTH.comment=How far the image adapts. 1 is roughly half way (eyes never fully adapt in a game).
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MIN=Auto Exposure Minimum
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MIN.comment=The darkest it may make the image (in bright views).
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MAX=Auto Exposure Maximum
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MAX.comment=The brightest it may make the image (in caves and at night).

# ---- W2: water
option.INTERACTIVE_RIPPLES=Interactive Ripples
option.INTERACTIVE_RIPPLES.comment=You, mobs and boats leave rings and wakes on the water around you (a small wave simulation, 64 blocks across).
option.CAUSTIC_DISPERSION=Caustic Dispersion
option.CAUSTIC_DISPERSION.comment=Colour fringes on the light patterns under water: each colour focuses at a slightly different depth, so the fringes widen deeper down. 1 is physically correct (subtle); higher exaggerates it.
value.CAUSTIC_DISPERSION.0.0=Off

# ---- W3: light volume and occlusion
option.SUN_BOUNCE=Sun Bounce
option.SUN_BOUNCE.comment=Sunlight bounced off sunlit blocks lights the shade nearby in their colour: green under trees, warm light from sand and terracotta, light reaching into cave mouths. Needs Coloured Lighting.
option.VOXEL_SKY_OCCLUSION=Sky Occlusion
option.VOXEL_SKY_OCCLUSION.comment=How much the sky light is shut out by the blocks around (overhangs, caves, dense trees), worked out from the blocks themselves rather than Minecraft's light levels alone. Needs Coloured Lighting.
option.DIRECTIONAL_BLOCKLIGHT=Directional Block Light
option.DIRECTIONAL_BLOCKLIGHT.comment=Faces turned away from a light source get less of its light; torches, lanterns and lava also glint on water and puddles. Needs Coloured Lighting.

option.MIST=Mist
option.MIST.comment=Mist that forms on still, humid nights, lies thickest around sunrise and burns off through the morning, also after rain and in swamps. It pools low and drifts with the wind; sunlight makes shafts in it.
value.MIST.0=Off
value.MIST.50=50%
value.MIST.100=100%
value.MIST.150=150%
value.MIST.200=200%
option.RAIN_CURTAINS=Rain Curtains
option.RAIN_CURTAINS.comment=Grey sheets of falling rain in the distance while it rains, moving with the clouds.
option.LIGHT_FOG=Light Fog
option.LIGHT_FOG.comment=Glowing haze around light sources (lava, torches, portals), strongest in caves and mist. Needs Coloured Lighting and Light Shaft Quality above Off.
option.WATER_SHAFTS_FROM_ABOVE=Water Shafts From Above
option.WATER_SHAFTS_FROM_ABOVE.comment=The light shafts under water also show, faintly, when looking into the water from above.
option.COMPACT_TAA_HISTORY=Compact TAA History
option.COMPACT_TAA_HISTORY.comment=Stores the TAA history at 11/10 bits per colour channel instead of 16: a little less memory traffic at high resolutions, but slow changes can stall and colours can drift slightly.
option.HALF_RES_SHADOWS=Half-Size Shadows
option.HALF_RES_SHADOWS.comment=Works out the soft sun shadows at half resolution (together with the ambient occlusion) and adds them up over frames: much faster at high resolutions, very slightly softer edges. Under glass and water the full path still runs.
